<!-- Yiḍ launcher glyph: a moth at night, drawn to a crescent moon, under
     a few stars. The moth is one even-odd path, wings folded into a triangle
     whose inner edges follow its slender body, plumed antennae, and a spot on
     each wing that shows the background. The stars have four points so they
     never read as those spots, and the moon stands apart from the moth, so
     the shapes stay distinct when the system tints them all in one colour as
     the themed icon. Everything sits inside the 66 dp safe zone.
     No fixed paint: the colours are dynamic palette resources, see
     res/values/colors.xml. As the monochrome layer the system replaces the
     tint anyway, so both the plain and the themed icon follow the wallpaper. -->
